# Project Rules & Tech Stack

## Tech Stack
- Frontend/Mobile: React Native with Expo (TypeScript)
- Navigation: Expo Router (file-based)
- Styling: NativeWind (Tailwind CSS for React Native)
- Backend & Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL, Auth, Storage, Edge Functions)
- AI Integration: OpenAI GPT-4o Vision via Supabase Edge Function only (never expose OPENAI_API_KEY in the client)

## UI / Screenshots (GLOBAL)
- **Screenshot-first for the whole app:** user screenshots are layout truth below `AppChromeHeader`.
- **Old code has no weight** — rebuild to match the screen; if mock conflicts with existing code, **mock wins** (no merge/hybrid).
- See `.cursor/rules/pixel-screens.mdc` for pixel-perfect process.

## Code Standards
- Use TypeScript for all components and functions.
- Keep components modular and reusable under `src/`.
- Handle loading and error states for all asynchronous operations (API calls, camera access, database queries).
- Do not use deprecated React Native components.
- Write clean code with clear naming conventions.
- Prefer mock AI mode (`EXPO_PUBLIC_USE_MOCK_AI=true`) when keys are missing so UI can be built without spend.
- Never commit `.env` files or secrets.
